<header class="site-header">
  <div class="bar">
    {#- The logo goes to the home page, as visitors and search engines expect.
        It used to go to the services page, which left one link on the whole
        site pointing at the home page. #}
    {%- set brandHref = '/' %}
    <a class="brand" href="{{ brandHref }}"
       aria-label="{{ site.company }}, home">
      {#- Both logos ship and CSS shows the right one, because the theme is now a
          runtime choice rather than something known at build time. The dark
          artwork is remapped (white letterforms, orange wordmark, transparent
          ground), not an inversion. #}
      <picture class="logo-light">
        <source srcset="/assets/logo.webp" type="image/webp">
        <img class="brand-logo" src="/assets/logo.png" width="225" height="124"
             alt="{{ site.company }}">
      </picture>
      <picture class="logo-dark" aria-hidden="true">
        <source srcset="/assets/logo-dark.webp" type="image/webp">
        <img class="brand-logo" src="/assets/logo-dark.png" width="225" height="124" alt="">
      </picture>
    </a>

    <input type="checkbox" id="navtoggle" class="navtoggle" hidden>
    <label for="navtoggle" class="navbtn" aria-hidden="true">Menu</label>

    <form id="sitesearch" class="sitesearch" role="search" hidden>
      <label class="visually-hidden" for="searchq">Search adicot.com</label>
      <input id="searchq" type="search" placeholder="Search calculators…" autocomplete="off"
             role="combobox" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="searchresults" aria-autocomplete="list">
      <ul id="searchresults" class="searchresults" role="listbox" aria-label="Search results" hidden></ul>
      <p id="searchstatus" class="visually-hidden" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    </form>

    {#- Two of these carry a mega menu. The top level is a real link in every
        case, so without JavaScript the nav still reaches /services and
        /calculators; the disclosure button beside it is revealed by nav.js and
        is the only part that needs scripting. Menu contents come from the same
        data the pages are built from, so a new category or service page appears
        here without anyone remembering to add it. -#}
    <nav class="mainnav" aria-label="Main">
      <ul>
        <li class="nav-has-menu">
          <a href="{{ site.servicesUrl }}"{% if "/services" in page.url %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>Engineering Services</a>
          <button type="button" class="nav-disclose" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="mm-services" hidden>
            <span class="visually-hidden">Engineering services menu</span>
            <span class="chev" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </button>
          <div class="megamenu" id="mm-services" hidden>
            <ul>
              {%- for item in services.items %}{% if item.page %}
              <li>
                <a href="/services/{{ item.slug }}">{{ item.name }}</a>
                <span>{{ item.summary | truncate(72) }}</span>
              </li>
              {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
              <li class="mm-all"><a href="{{ site.servicesUrl }}">All engineering services &rarr;</a></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </li>

        <li class="nav-has-menu">
          <a href="/calculators"{% if page.url == "/calculators.html" %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>Calculators</a>
          <button type="button" class="nav-disclose" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="mm-calcs" hidden>
            <span class="visually-hidden">Calculators menu</span>
            <span class="chev" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </button>
          <div class="megamenu megamenu-wide" id="mm-calcs" hidden>
            <ul>
              {%- for group in taxonomy %}
              <li>
                <a href="/calculators#{{ group.name | slugify }}">{{ group.name }}</a>
                <span>{{ group.items | length }} calculator{% if group.items | length != 1 %}s{% endif %}</span>
              </li>
              {%- endfor %}
              <li class="mm-updates">
                <a href="/calculator-updates">Calculator Updates</a>
                <span>New calculators and corrections, by email</span>
              </li>
              <li class="mm-all"><a href="/calculators">See all {{ calculatorCount }} calculators &rarr;</a></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </li>

        <li><a href="/about"{% if page.url == "/about.html" %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>About</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog"{% if "/blog" in page.url %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>Blog</a></li>
        <li><a href="/contact"{% if page.url == "/contact.html" %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>Contact</a></li>
        {#- The two actions sit at the end, the primary one last. Updates is secondary
            to Get a Quote, so outlined rather than filled: two solid buttons side by
            side compete instead of ranking. Its label says what you get, since
            "Updates" alone did not say it was a signup. -#}
        <li><a class="nav-sub" href="/calculator-updates" title="Email when a calculator is added or corrected">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" fill="none"
               stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <rect x="2.5" y="5" width="19" height="14" rx="2"/><path d="m3 6.5 9 6 9-6"/>
          </svg>Get Calculator Updates</a></li>
        <li><a class="nav-cta" href="{{ site.quoteUrl }}">{{ site.quoteLabel }}</a></li>
        {#- Light/dark switch, last. It shows where it takes you, as an icon and a
            word ("Dark" in light mode, "Light" in dark mode), which reads more
            plainly than an icon of the current state. Revealed by theme.js:
            without JavaScript it cannot do anything, so it should not be there. #}
        <li class="nav-theme"><button type="button" id="themetoggle" class="themetoggle" hidden>
          <svg class="icon-moon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" fill="none"
               stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M20.5 14.5A8.5 8.5 0 0 1 9.5 3.5a8.5 8.5 0 1 0 11 11z"/>
          </svg>
          <svg class="icon-sun" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" fill="none"
               stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4.2"/>
            <path d="M12 2v2.5M12 19.5V22M2 12h2.5M19.5 12H22M4.9 4.9l1.8 1.8M17.3 17.3l1.8 1.8M4.9 19.1l1.8-1.8M17.3 6.7l1.8-1.8"/>
          </svg>
          <span class="theme-label">Dark</span>
        </button></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>
